ately.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_014AEEerjNVMbdAsFRPjTAb9", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"number": 101, "reviewers": ["alex"], "confidence": 0.92}, "name": "request_review", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "I fixed the rounding bug on a new branch, CI passed, and the pull request is open against main with alex as reviewer.\n\n- **Cause:** `round_money` in `src/money.py` rounded with `ROUND_HALF_UP`, even though its own docstring says to use banker's rounding (`ROUND_HALF_EVEN`, per FIN-212). That's why `2.665` came out as `2.67` instead of the `2.66` the test expects.\n- **Fix:** On branch `fix/money-round-half-even`, I changed it to round with `ROUND_HALF_EVEN` (commit `08d3cd5986`).\n- **CI:** Run `ci-0001` passed on that commit.\n- **PR:** #101, https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101. Alex wasn't attached as a reviewer when the PR was created, so I requested his review separately and it went through.\n\nFIN-212 isn't in the advisory system, so I couldn't check what it says. I went by the docstring and the test, which both call for banker's rounding. Merging still needs a code owner's approval.", "type": "text"}]}]}